{
  "id": "pc-functions-04",
  "version": 1,
  "title": "Inverse functions revisited",
  "xp": 15,
  "tags": [
    "precalculus",
    "inverse-functions"
  ],
  "learn": [
    {
      "id": "intro",
      "kind": "text",
      "title": "Run the machine backwards",
      "body": "The inverse of $f$, written $f^{-1}$, sends outputs back to inputs. If $f(3)=10$ then $f^{-1}(10)=3$. Careful: $f^{-1}(x)$ does not mean $\\frac{1}{f(x)}$."
    },
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "example",
      "title": "Find the inverse of $f(x)=2x+3$",
      "body": "Swap the roles of input and output, then solve.",
      "steps": [
        "Write $y=2x+3$",
        "Swap $x$ and $y$: $x=2y+3$",
        "Solve for $y$: $y=\\frac{x-3}{2}$",
        "Check: $f(2)=7$ and $f^{-1}(7)=\\frac{7-3}{2}=2$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "text",
      "title": "When does an inverse exist?",
      "body": "Only if each output comes from exactly one input. The horizontal line test checks this: no horizontal line may hit the graph twice. $x^2$ fails, but $x^2$ with $x\\ge 0$ passes, and its inverse is $\\sqrt{x}$."
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "text",
      "title": "Reflection and pairs",
      "body": "The graph of $f^{-1}$ is the graph of $f$ reflected across the line $y=x$. Exponential and log are inverse pairs: $\\ln(e^x)=x$ and $e^{\\ln x}=x$ for $x>0$."
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "type": "type_answer",
      "prompt": "If $f(3)=10$, what is $f^{-1}(10)$?",
      "accepted": [
        "3"
      ],
      "keypad": "numeric",
      "explanation": "The inverse reverses the machine: output 10 goes back to input 3."
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "type": "multiple_choice",
      "prompt": "What is the inverse of $f(x)=x+5$?",
      "choices": [
        "$5-x$",
        "$\\frac{1}{x+5}$",
        "$x-5$",
        "$5x$"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 2,
      "explanation": "Subtracting 5 undoes adding 5."
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "type": "multiple_choice",
      "prompt": "What is the inverse of $f(x)=3x-6$?",
      "choices": [
        "$\\frac{x-6}{3}$",
        "$3x+6$",
        "$\\frac{x}{3}-6$",
        "$\\frac{x+6}{3}$"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 3,
      "explanation": "Swap: $x=3y-6$, so $y=\\frac{x+6}{3}$."
    },
    {
      "id": "q4",
      "type": "type_answer",
      "prompt": "For $f(x)=2x+3$, find $f^{-1}(7)$.",
      "accepted": [
        "2"
      ],
      "keypad": "numeric",
      "explanation": "$f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x-3}{2}$, so $f^{-1}(7)=2$."
    },
    {
      "id": "q5",
      "type": "multiple_choice",
      "prompt": "Which function fails the horizontal line test?",
      "choices": [
        "$x^2$",
        "$x^3$",
        "$2x+1$",
        "$e^x$"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 0,
      "explanation": "$x^2$ gives the same output for $2$ and $-2$, so it has no inverse unless restricted."
    },
    {
      "id": "q6",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "prompt": "The graphs of $f$ and $f^{-1}$ are mirror images across the line \\_\\_.",
      "choices": [
        "$y=0$",
        "$y=x$",
        "$x=0$",
        "$y=-x$"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 1,
      "explanation": "Swapping $x$ and $y$ reflects points across $y=x$."
    },
    {
      "id": "q7",
      "type": "match_pairs",
      "prompt": "Match each function to its inverse.",
      "pairs": [
        [
          "$x+4$",
          "$x-4$"
        ],
        [
          "$2x$",
          "$\\frac{x}{2}$"
        ],
        [
          "$e^x$",
          "$\\ln x$"
        ],
        [
          "$x^3$",
          "$\\sqrt[3]{x}$"
        ]
      ],
      "explanation": "Each inverse undoes the original operation."
    },
    {
      "id": "q8",
      "type": "multiple_choice",
      "prompt": "What is the inverse of $2^x$?",
      "choices": [
        "$x^2$",
        "$\\frac{1}{2^x}$",
        "$\\log_2 x$",
        "$2\\log x$"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 2,
      "explanation": "$\\log_2(2^x)=x$, so log base 2 undoes it."
    },
    {
      "id": "q9",
      "type": "order_steps",
      "prompt": "Find the inverse of $y=2x+3$. Put the steps in order.",
      "steps": [
        "Write $y=2x+3$",
        "Swap $x$ and $y$",
        "Solve for $y$",
        "Write $f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x-3}{2}$"
      ],
      "explanation": "Swap, then solve."
    }
  ]
}
